 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Bundle options documentation\nDescription: Documentation for SAP Field Service Management and SAP Cloud ALM bundle options is now available.  For more information, see SAP Field Service Management Bundle and SAP Cloud ALM Bundle.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1155 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Central store logs display source entity ID\nDescription: The central store logs display the source entity ID, which represents the group ID in the Identity Directory.  For more information, see Monitor Central Store Logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1156 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Download all updated entities for a provisioning job\nDescription: You can now download and view the details of all updated entities by a provisioning job. To enable this, set the properties ips.trace.updated.entity and ips.trace.updated.entity.content to true.  For more information, see Manage Provisioning Job Logs and List of Properties.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1157 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: OAuth Client Authentication\nDescription: The Add JSON Web Token UI has bee changed. Now you can manually configure the issuer or choose from OpenID Connect compliant corporate identity providers. See Configure JWT for OAuth Client Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1158 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1159 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Applications - default transformations changes\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP Ariba Applications are enhanced with the expression preserveArrayWithSingleElement set to true. The transformation mappings for the attribute plant are excluded from the default write and proxy write transformations, since the attribute's value cannot be created with POST and PUT or PATCH request anymore.  For more information, see:     SAP Ariba Applications (Source)  SAP Ariba Applications (Target)  SAP Ariba Applications (Proxy)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1160 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Applications - default transformations changes\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP Ariba Applications are now enhanced with the expression preserveArrayWithSingleElement set to true. The transformation mappings for the attribute plant are excluded from the default write and proxy write transformations, since the attribute's value cannot be created with POST and PUT or PATCH request anymore.  For more information, see", "\nVersion: 27643\n\n--- Record 1160 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Applications - default transformations changes\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP Ariba Applications are now enhanced with the expression preserveArrayWithSingleElement set to true. The transformation mappings for the attribute plant are excluded from the default write and proxy write transformations, since the attribute's value cannot be created with POST and PUT or PATCH request anymore.  For more information, see:     SAP Ariba Applications (Source)  SAP Ariba Applications (Target)  SAP Ariba Applications (Proxy)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-25\nValid as Of: 2025-03-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 731 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Custom Rules Available\nDescription: In the configuration manager, you can now create custom rules for message interchange to enable the agreement lookup in the Partner Directory.   Creating a custom rule also involves creating custom keys and activating the custom rule. See Configuration Manager.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-08\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 732 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Authorization\nDescription: The following new role templates for working with interchanges have been added:       B2bInterchangeRead allows you to read interchanges without payloads.      B2bInterchangePayloadRead allows you to read interchange payloads.      B2bInterchangeOperate allows you to execute operational tasks (retry, restart, and cancel) for interchanges.      To learn how these role templates are included in the existing role collections, see Identity and Access Management for Trading Partner Management and Monitor Interchanges.  In the SAP BTP cockpit, you can also assign these role templates to your user separately.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 733 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 6.66.*  Increment: 2504  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-01\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 734 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Analytical Insights Capability - Support for SAP Datasphere analytic models in an SAP Business Data Cloud formation.\nDescription: Analytic models from SAP Datasphere are now supported by the analytical insights capability in Joule. Your SAP Datasphere system must be part of an SAP Business Data Cloud formation that includes your SAP Analytics Cloud system and Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 735 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Checking sales order fulfillment status in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule allows you to check whether a sales order's fulfillment is on track and identify the issues that block its fulfillment. For each sales order, Joule can tell whether such issues exist in the order processing phase. If yes, you can display issue details, view possible causes and handling suggestions for each issue, and navigate to related apps.  For more information on this capability, see Sales Order Status Check.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Sales\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-30\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 736 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Expiring Prices Handling in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now enables you to manage expiring prices (stored as condition records for pricing in sales) in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition. With Joule, you can fetch prices that will expire soon, extend their valid-to dates, and adjust their condition amounts or ratios as you need.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Sales\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-30\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 737 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Available in SAP SuccessFactors Mobile apps\nDescription: You can now use Joule, SAP's AI copilot, inSAP SuccessFactors Mobile apps. For more information, see Joule Available in SAP SuccessFactors Mobile\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 738 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Now Available in SAP Digital Manufacturing\nDescription: Joule is now available in SAP Digital Manufacturing for informational use cases. You have conversational access to the product documentation for SAP Digital Manufacturing. Just enter your query or question in plain natural language, and Joule searches the product documentation to find the answer. Joule summarizes the search results in the background. This summarization is then displayed to you as the answer to your question, along with the top three search results. If you select the title link of a result, you're taken directly to the relevant topic on SAP Help Portal.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 739 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Transactional Use Cases are now Enabled for Cash Management Capabilities in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: You can now use Joule to provide comprehensive cash management capabilities, including monitoring", " General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 739 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Transactional Use Cases are now Enabled for Cash Management Capabilities in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: You can now use Joule to provide comprehensive cash management capabilities, including monitoring bank statements, analyzing cash flow, and initiating bank transfers. This feature is essential for efficiently managing finances, identifying cash shortages, and maintaining a clear overview of financial activities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 740 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Case Now Supported for Field Logistics in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional use case is now supported in Field Logistics for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:      Fetch Quantity for a Non-Stock Item    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2591 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-17\nVersion: 26387\n\n--- Record 2592 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Advanced Financial Closing - group mapping\nDescription: The default read and proxy read transformations of SAP Advanced Financial Closing provisioning systems are extended to support the provisioning of application-specific groups.  These tr