nt Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3410 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for businessCard Documents in AWS region Australia (Sydney)\nDescription: The businessCard documents are now supported in the AWS region Australia (Sydney).  See Supported Document Types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1651 ---\nComponent: Integration Suite General Features\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Integration Suite Documentation Survey\nDescription: Help us improve the SAP Integration Suite documentation by sharing your experience. Please take a moment to complete this short survey.  We'd love to hear from you!\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-11\nValid as Of: 2025-01-11\nVersion: 2412\n\n--- Record 1652 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Effort Estimation Data in Scenario Evaluation Reports\nDescription: You can now access effort estimation data in your scenario evaluation spreadsheet exports.  For information on creating scenario evaluation reports, check Create a Scenario Evaluation Request .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-11\nValid as Of: 2025-01-11\nVersion: 2412\n\n--- Record 1653 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Performance Data for Integration Scenarios\nDescription: Performance details, such as message sizes and processing times, are now available for each scenario in the scenario evaluation spreadsheet export.Note  To access these details in your data extraction, ensure performance data collection is enabled on your PO System and perform a new data ex